            <ArticleTitle>Acute effects of tai chi exercise on cardiac autonomic function in healthy adults with tai chi experience.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>226-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>About 1 in 3 American adults have cardiovascular disease associated with risk factors such as physical inactivity, obesity, and stress. Heart rate variability (HRV) analysis is considered a non-invasive procedure for analyzing cardiovascular autonomic influence. Depressed HRV has been linked to abnormal cardiovascular autonomic modulation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
